 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "Musa is a 'prophet' drop; his companion is an 'honored' drop labelled Yusha' bin Nun (both tafsirs name him). The fish comes alive and slips into the sea at the word that states it (Al-Muyassar). They rest at the rock at dusk (As-Sa'di: the night sheltered them there), walk on, then return to the rock. Cover title uses Al-Muyassar's 'ملتقى البحرين' because the plan title repeats Quran wording (مجمع البحرين) and the verifier rejects it."
